claim.claim-text:
an active grille shutter system (10; 100; 200) having a frame (12) located in a cooling pathway (16) of a power source for a vehicle, wherein the frame (12) includes a base integrated end cap (14b) and a base non-integrated end cap (14d), wherein the base non-integrated end cap has an actuator pocket (18);
a plurality of vanes (32a, 32b, 32c) rotatably connected at a first end to the base end cap and extending across the cooling pathway (16) and connected at a second end to the base non-integrated end cap (14d), wherein the plurality of vanes (32a, 32b, 32c) rotate between an open position and a closed position; and
an actuator (30) having a housing (38) with a rotatable output formed in the housing (38);
one or more datum features (33a, 33b, 33c, 33d, 33e, 33f) extending from the housing (38) of the actuator (30); and
one or more datum cavities (34a, 34b, 34c, 34d, 34e, 34f) formed in the actuator pocket (18) of the base integrated end cap (14b) for receiving a respective one of the one or more datum features (33a, 33b, 33c, 33d, 33e, 33f) for aligning the housing (38) of the actuator (30) during assembly to the actuator (30) to the actuator pocket (18) and preventing rotation of the housing (38) of the actuator (30) during operation.
